    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d674">

                <pb facs="0819" n="723" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg723"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/8674: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting President of the Technical Board</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harbin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-06-01T10:00:00+08:26"><hi rendition="#italic">June 1, 1921—10
                                a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received June 3—1:14 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>… Negotiations in progress between the Chita government and the Kappel leaders
                    which [<hi rendition="#italic">will?</hi>] undoubtedly lead to understanding
                    thus eliminating Semenoff.</p>
                <p>Referring to my cable of May 13, 4 p.m.,<anchor n="32" xml:id="d674-f1"/> no
                    particular change in the Chinese Eastern situation. Export movement continues
                    unmolested via Vladivostok. Persistent rumors here that Japanese banks prepared
                    to advance two and a half million yen to the Chinese Eastern about June 10,
                    presumably on arrangement with the Chinese Minister of Finance. No details as to
                    terms.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
